{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the two Dart estimate paths now price the same request differently by the system prompt**

This dangling fallback prices known input at `(inputChars + systemPromptChars) / 4`, but the sibling estimated path in `_foldAssistant` (an assistant message that landed with provider-omitted usage, paired to the same `_PendingSummary`) still prices input at `summary.inputChars / 4` — the system prompt is excluded there. So the identical request contributes `systemPromptChars/4` more tokens when it dangles than when it finalizes unreported. Presumably frozen deliberately by the AC2 byte-identity guarantee (changing `_foldAssistant` would alter completed-chain artifacts), which is a defensible call — but worth a comment on `_PendingSummary` naming the asymmetry as intentional, or a follow-up that fixes both paths together under a schema bump so a future reader doesn't treat one of them as the bug it isn't (or is).
